graph TB
  D["DELETE one key from a binary search tree<br/>first search for the node that holds it, then repair the links"]
  D --> C1["CASE 1<br/>the node is a leaf"]
  D --> C2["CASE 2<br/>the node has exactly one child"]
  D --> C3["CASE 3<br/>the node has two children"]
  C1 --> C1a["ACTION<br/>detach the node and set the parent link that pointed at it to empty"]
  C2 --> C2a["ACTION<br/>splice the only child into the parent link, so the subtree is lifted by one"]
  C3 --> C3a["ACTION<br/>find the in-order successor, the leftmost node of the right subtree"]
  C3a --> C3b["copy the successor key into the node being deleted"]
  C3b --> C3c["then delete the successor from the right subtree, which is case 1 or case 2"]
  C1a ~~~ WHY
  WHY["WHY THE SUCCESSOR<br/>it is the next key in sorted order, so moving its key up keeps every left key smaller and every right key larger"]
